[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":263},["ShallowReactive",2],{"news:\u002Fnews\u002F2012-03-17-future-use-of-maintainer-in-details":3,"news-timeline":44},{"id":4,"title":5,"author":6,"body":7,"date":34,"description":35,"extension":36,"meta":37,"navigation":38,"path":39,"readingTime":40,"seo":41,"stem":42,"__hash__":43},"news\u002Fnews\u002F2012-03-17-future-use-of-maintainer-in-details.md","Future use of MAINTAINER= in DETAILS","wdp",{"type":8,"value":9,"toc":30},"minimark",[10,14,17,24,27],[11,12,13],"p",{},"Currently we aren't using the MAINTAINER= flag correctly in Lunar. I'd even go that far and say, we don't care about that flag and we simply ignore it. With the new separation (stable \u002F unstable) this will change:",[11,15,16],{},"The maintainer-flag is usually set by developers or people for a specific module; that means such people or developer have a special need or knowledge about that module and should be asked whenever there's an update or modification to this specific module.",[11,18,19,20,23],{},"For example:",[21,22],"br",{},"\nEl_Angelo is set as maintainer for xorg-server, that's because he's reading the maillinglists, checking their bugtracker and he knows what he's doing regarding xorg (At least, thats my impression) - If someone else wants to update xorg-server he\u002Fshe should ask El_Angelo first why he didn't update it, yet. Because El_Angelo might have a good reason for not doing so.",[11,25,26],{},"That means from now on we will care for the MAINTAINER flag and everytime a module needs a modification or update the MAINTAINER has to be contacted first. If a Maintainer doesn't respond within two weeks, you can update or modify the module yourself. If it's _really_ important to update something (bugfix, security patch) you might wait less time; However: Please always try to contact the maintainer, you can assume, that the Maintainer knows better about the module than you do.",[11,28,29],{},"We've started some sort of mass-mailing to all set MAINTAINER's in Lunar Linux with a list of the modules they've set themselves as MAINTAINER and hope to get a lot of feedback. We will remove all MAINTAINER flags from users who didn't respond within two weeks.",{"title":31,"searchDepth":32,"depth":32,"links":33},"",3,[],"2012-03-17","The MAINTAINER field in DETAILS starts to matter: ask a module's maintainer before changing it.","md",{},true,"\u002Fnews\u002F2012-03-17-future-use-of-maintainer-in-details",2,{"title":5,"description":35},"news\u002F2012-03-17-future-use-of-maintainer-in-details","EUUbpTTlvJB0sxTD37r93O-m3GnQ43oSsJS6x7L0OWg",[45,49,53,57,61,65,69,73,77,81,85,86,89,93,97,101,105,108,112,116,120,124,128,132,136,140,144,148,152,156,160,164,168,172,176,180,184,188,192,196,200,204,208,212,216,220,224,228,232,236,240,244,248,252,255,259],{"title":46,"path":47,"date":48},"Moving towards a more aggressive release cycle","\u002Fnews\u002F2023-08-13-moving-towards-a-more-aggressive-release-cycle","2023-08-13",{"title":50,"path":51,"date":52},"We are moving to libera.chat network","\u002Fnews\u002F2021-05-23-we-are-moving-to-libera-chat-network","2021-05-23",{"title":54,"path":55,"date":56},"We are still very much alive","\u002Fnews\u002F2017-10-18-we-are-still-very-much-alive","2017-10-18",{"title":58,"path":59,"date":60},"Lunar Linux 1.7.0 (i686 & x86_64) ISO’s released","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-10-11-lunar-linux-1-7-0-i686-and-x86-64-isos-released","2014-10-11",{"title":62,"path":63,"date":64},"Lunar Linux 1.7.0-rc2 (i686 & x86_64) ISO’s released","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-09-16-lunar-linux-1-7-0-rc2-i686-and-x86-64-isos-released","2014-09-16",{"title":66,"path":67,"date":68},"Service transition","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-05-24-service-transition","2014-05-24",{"title":70,"path":71,"date":72},"Services from lunar-linux.org may be disrupted","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-05-19-services-from-lunar-linux-org-may-be-disrupted","2014-05-19",{"title":74,"path":75,"date":76},"New installation ISO development","\u002Fnews\u002F2013-09-19-new